    {
      "id": "pandas-essentials.p1",
      "title": "pandas - Load, Filter, Group",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "title",
          "text": "pandas - Load, Filter, Group",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 38,
            "minFontSize": 29,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.16
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.title"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "1. Loading Data",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.s1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Most pandas memory problems are created on the read line.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b1"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "usecols",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - read only the columns you need."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "dtype",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - stop silent object columns."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "parse_dates",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - parse once, at read time."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "chunksize",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - iterate when the file will not fit."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "gap": 20.32999999999998,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "2. Selecting & Filtering",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.s2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Four ways to select. Mixing them is where SettingWithCopyWarning comes from.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b3"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            ".loc slices are inclusive of the end label; .iloc is not.",
            "Combine masks with & | ~ and parenthesise every comparison.",
            ".query() reads well and avoids temporaries on big frames."
          ],
          "gap": 24,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "3. groupby: split-apply-combine",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.s3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Pick the verb by the shape you want back.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b5"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "agg",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - one row per group."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "transform",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - same shape as the input, broadcast back."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "filter",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - drop whole groups."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "apply",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - anything else, and slow."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "gap": 20.329999999999966,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "4. merge",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.s4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A merge is a SQL join with the same fan-out risk and worse defaults.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b7"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "validate=",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - '1:1', '1:m', 'm:1' - raises on surprise duplicates."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "indicator=True",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - adds _merge: left_only / both / right_only."
              }
            ],
            "join() is merge on the index; concat() stacks, it does not match."
          ],
          "gap": 24,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b8"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "df = pd.read_csv(\"sales.csv\",\n    usecols=[\"id\", \"region\", \"amt\", \"d\"],\n    dtype={\"id\": \"int32\", \"region\": \"category\"},\n    parse_dates=[\"d\"], na_values=[\"\", \"NA\"])\ndf.info(memory_usage=\"deep\")",
          "title": "Example - read_csv",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 16,
            "lineHeight": 1.35,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 14
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b9"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "columns": [
            "Accessor",
            "Indexed by",
            "End"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              ".loc[]",
              "labels / mask",
              "inclusive"
            ],
            [
              ".iloc[]",
              "positions",
              "exclusive"
            ],
            [
              "mask",
              "boolean Series",
              "n/a"
            ],
            [
              ".query()",
              "string expression",
              "n/a"
            ]
          ],
          "widths": [
            0.28,
            0.45,
            0.27
          ],
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 17,
            "lineHeight": 1.25,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 16
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b10"
        },
        {
          "type": "box",
          "variant": "warning",
          "title": "Common trap",
          "text": "df[df.a > 1][\"b\"] = 0 writes to a copy - SettingWithCopyWarning.\nDo it in one step: df.loc[df.a > 1, \"b\"] = 0",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 18,
            "lineHeight": 1.25,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 16
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b11"
        },
        {
          "id": "split-apply-combine",
          "type": "diagram",
          "family": "sequence",
          "preset": "steps",
          "direction": "horizontal",
          "link": "arrow",
          "items": [
            "Split",
            "Apply",
            "Combine"
          ],
          "caption": "What groupby actually does",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 19,
            "lineHeight": 1.33,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 16
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "df.groupby(\"region\", as_index=False).agg(\n    n=(\"amt\", \"size\"),\n    total=(\"amt\", \"sum\"),\n    avg=(\"amt\", \"mean\"))\n\ndf[\"pct\"] = df.amt / df.groupby(\"region\").amt.transform(\"sum\")",
          "title": "Example - named agg and transform",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 16,
            "lineHeight": 1.35,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 14
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b12"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "out = df.merge(dim, on=\"id\", how=\"left\",\n               validate=\"m:1\", indicator=True)\nout._merge.value_counts()  # check before dropping it",
          "title": "Example - validated left merge",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 16,
            "lineHeight": 1.35,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 14
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b13"
        },
        {
          "type": "box",
          "variant": "warning",
          "title": "Common trap",
          "text": "Duplicate keys on the right side multiply rows silently.\nhow='left' keeps rows but fills unmatched columns with NaN - which quietly upcasts ints to float.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 18,
            "lineHeight": 1.25,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 16
          },
          "id": "pandas-essentials.p1.b14"
        }
      ],
